Syntax: toxicity

This passive skill represents a thief's knowledge of poisons and toxic substances.
The higher your toxicity skill, the more resistant you become to poisons. As the 
application of poisons sometimes leans on the application of other dangerous 
substances, thieves with this training will also find themselves more resistant 
to sleep, disease, paralysis, and acid.

Notably, this built-up resistance will aid the thief in the planting and preparation of
poisons using the planting and cooking skills.

Toxicity provides several benefits:
- Increased resistance to poison effects
- Partial resistance to sleep, disease, paralysis, and acid effects
- Reduced chance of self-poisoning when using the poison weapons skill
- Enhanced protection when harvesting dangerous reagents
- Improved effectiveness when creating poisons through cooking

This skill improves passively as you are exposed to toxic substances and
as you work with poisons. Higher levels of thief training will increase
your maximum potential in this skill.

